[style name="Interaction_Style"]
if {Dead_person_choice} == 1:
	join Town_Leader rightmost
	Town_Leader: Thorinn, you’ve saved them! Truly, you are a gift to Rockfall!
	Malrik: *Malric whispers from the shadows* Psst.
	join Thorinn (normal) leftmost
	Malrik: What will you do now doctor...?
	- Publicly credit Malric
		Thorinn: This cure wasn’t mine alone. Malric’s knowledge made this possible.
		Town_Leader: Malric...?
	- Accept the credit
		Thorinn (normal): I just did what had to be done.
	- Thank Malric in private
		Thorinn: I just did what had to be done.
		leave Town_Leader
		Thorinn: *Turning to Malric in the shadows* So...listen.
		join Malrik rightmost
		Thorinn: I didn’t mention you, but know this—you have my thanks.
		Malrik: Wise choice, doctor. But secrets weigh heavy.
elif {Dead_person_choice} == 2:
	join Town_Leader rightmost
	Town_Leader: Thorinn, you tried your best, but this time it was not enough. Look at this loss.
	Malrik: *Malric whispers from the shadows* Psst.
	join Thorinn leftmost
	Malrik: What will you do now doctor...?
	- Admit fault
		Thorinn (agitated): I really did the best I could.
		Malrik: Better luck next time!
	- Publicly blame Malric
		Thorinn: This failure wasn’t mine alone. Malric’s evil ways made this possible.
		Town_Leader: Malric...?!
		Malrik: ...!
	- Confront Malric in private
		Thorinn (agitated): I really did the best I could.
		leave Town_Leader
		Thorinn (agitated): *Turning to Malric in the shadows* So...listen.
		join Malrik rightmost
		Thorinn: I didn'’t expose you, but know this—you also had a hand in this failure.
		Malrik: That was a wise choice, doctor. But secrets weigh heavy.
elif {Dead_person_choice} == 3:
	join Town_Leader rightmost
	Town_Leader: Thorinn, you tried your best! Such a shame, now leave these poor souls to rest!
	Malrik: *Malric whispers from the shadows* Psst.
	join Thorinn leftmost
	What will you do now doctor...?
	- Accept the credit
		Thorinn: I just did what had to be done.
		Malrik: ...
	- Publicly credit Malric
		Thorinn: This cure wasn’t mine alone. Malric’s knowledge made this possible.
		Town_Leader: Malric...?
	- Thank Malric in private
		Thorinn: I just did what had to be done.
		leave Town_Leader
		*Turning to Malric in the shadows* So...listen.
		join Malrik rightmost
		Thorinn: I didn’t mention you, but know this—you have my thanks.
		Malrik: Wise choice, doctor. But secrets weigh heavy.
elif {Dead_person_choice} == 4:
	join Town_Leader rightmost
	Town_Leader: Thorinn, you came with hope and promises, but we are left with grief. Five lives were lost under your care.
	Malrik: *Malric whispers from the shadows* Psst.
	join Thorinn (agitated) leftmost
	Malrik: Seems like your good intentions weren’t of much help this time. What will you tell them now?
	- Admit fault
		Thorinn (agitated): I have failed you, and I will not try to hide it. I... have no excuse for what happened. But let me prove that I can do better.
		Malrik: Hehe...Better luck next time!
	- Publicly blame Malric
		Thorinn (surprised): I know I failed, but I cannot shoulder all the blame for what has happened. Because Malric’s evil ways made this possible.
		Town_Leader: Malric...?!!
		Malrik: ...
	- Blame Malric in private
		Thorinn (agitated): I have failed you, and I will not try to hide it. I... have no excuse for what has happened. But let me prove that I can do better, that I can be worthy of your trust.
		leave Town_Leader
		Thorinn: *Turning to Malric in the shadows* So...listen.
		join Malrik rightmost
		Thorinn: I didn’t expose you, but know this—I will remember that you also had a hand in this failure.
